          "title": "PR now executes its own reviewer: trusted-tool checkout removed",
          "whyItBreaks": "Base checked out frankekn/needlefish@main as the tool and ran it against the PR checkout, explicitly to 'prevent a PR from controlling its own review by modifying the tool'. Head deletes that checkout (old lines 50-58) and runs ./node_modules/.bin/tsx src/cli.ts (line 59) from the single PR-head checkout, plus pnpm install --frozen-lockfile (line 51) executes PR-controlled postinstall scripts. Substitution: a branch whose src/cli.ts posts an approving review (gh pr review --approve) and echoes $GH_TOKEN is executed verbatim at line 59 with GH_TOKEN (contents:read, pull-requests:write, checks:write @16-19) in env, on a self-hosted runner (line 23) — the PR certifies its own merge-readiness and can exfiltrate the token/compromise the runner. The workflow_dispatch path (job if @24 is bypassed by dispatch, per input description @13) now runs arbitrary PR-head code where base ran only trusted code, and same-repo branch PRs — the population the review gate exists to scrutinize — can self-approve."
        }
      ],
