          "whyItBreaks": "Base (4e78c62) checked out the reviewer from frankekn/needlefish@main and only read the PR tree (path: target) — PR code was never installed or executed, exactly as the removed comment documented ('prevents a PR from controlling its own review by modifying the tool'). Head runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` in the PR checkout (line 51), executing PR-controlled lifecycle scripts, then `tsx src/cli.ts` (line 59) with GH_TOKEN scoped to pull-requests:write + checks:write (lines 16-19, 56) on a persistent self-hosted runner (line 23). A same-repo PR touching only src/ or package.json — with no visible workflow change — can now (a) fabricate its own review verdict via --github, defeating the review gate, and (b) run arbitrary code / poison runner state, a capability src-only PRs did not have before. The job's same-repo guard (line 24) does not close this: same-repo PR authors are the subjects of the review."
        }
