          "title": "Reviewer now executed from untrusted PR head; PR can forge its own review",
          "whyItBreaks": "The base workflow's own comment stated the trusted-tool pattern 'prevents a PR from controlling its own review by modifying the tool.' This diff removes the `Checkout trusted tool (main)` step and switches execution to the PR head: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` (line 51) and `./node_modules/.bin/tsx src/cli.ts` (line 59) now run entirely from the PR-head checkout that lines 43-47 place at the workspace root. The job's `if:` guard (line 24) only excludes fork PRs — a same-repo branch PR (pushable by anyone with branch write, not necessarily merge approval) can (a) modify src/cli.ts so the 'reviewer' posts an approving review/check, bypassing the merge gate, and (b) add a lifecycle-script dependency to package.json/pnpm-lock.yaml, executed at line 51 — previously install ran only in the trusted needlefish/ checkout and PR code was never installed or executed. All of this runs on `runs-on: self-hosted` (line 23, a persistent runner GitHub documents as unsafe for untrusted code) with GH_TOKEN granted `pull-requests: write` + `checks: write` (lines 18-19, 56). This is a merge-gate bypass plus arbitrary code execution introduced by this diff."
        }
